                <pb facs="0680" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-12T11:00:00+08:00">March 12, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 12—5:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>329. Following from the American Consul General, Mukden: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item><quote rend="blockquote">“March 11, noon. The principal officials of
                                the new government, appointed by the Regent on March 10th, are as
                                reported in my despatch of March 7th except Chang Ching-hui who is head of the
                                councilors Yuan or Privy
                                Council. Other members of the Privy Council are Tang Yu-lin, Yuan Chin-kai, Chang Hai-peng, Lo Cheng-yu and Kuei Fu. Chao Hsin-po was appointed Chief of the Legislative
                                    Yuan.”</quote></item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Other important officials mentioned in despatch of March 7th, referred
                            to above, are: Cheng Hsiao-hsu,
                            Premier; Hsi Hsia, Minister of
                            Finance and Governor of Kirin; Ma
                                Chan-shan, Minister of War and Governor of Heilungkiang;
                                Tsang Shih-yi, Minister of
                            Civil Administration and Governor of Fengtien; Hsieh Chieh-shih, Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
